1. Purpose & Architecture
--------------------------------------------------------------------

RSS-BOOKSTORE is an unprivileged, local-first power-user Manifest V3
Chromium extension and Python Native Messaging host that saves RSS/Atom
feed entries as browser bookmarks and mirrors them to a local Windows
folder as .url shortcut files with optional bidirectional synchronization.

The package is explicitly designed with the following invariants:
  * Local-First Architecture (INV-LOCAL-01): Network access is strictly limited
    to user-configured RSS/Atom feed endpoints with per-feed optional host
    permissions; no telemetry, no tracking, and no external cloud relays.
  * Unprivileged user-space execution (INV-LOCAL-02): RunAsInvoker non-elevation;
    the Native Messaging host registers under HKCU (current user) by default
    without requiring administrator privileges.
  * Zero External Runtime Dependencies (INV-LOCAL-03): Pure Chromium extension
    APIs and Python standard library; zero third-party npm runtime dependencies
    and zero third-party pip runtime dependencies.
  * Non-destructive bidirectional sync (INV-LOCAL-04): Preserves user bookmarks
    and .url files with safe atomic writes and ETag/Last-Modified HTTP caching.
  * Open standard interoperability (INV-LOCAL-05): Native OPML import/export
    and standard Windows Internet Shortcut (.url) format.
  * Zero Copyleft on processed feeds and bookmarks (INV-LOCAL-08): 100% MIT
    license with unencumbered user data ownership.
  * 100% Bilingual Documentation parity (INV-LOCAL-09): Full German (README_de.md)
    and English (README.md) documentation.
  * Documented 48-hour security disclosure response SLA (INV-LOCAL-10).

